WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.522
Production cleaning pipelines often need lineage fields.

00:00:03.522 --> 00:00:07.282
Source ID links the prepared row back to the raw record.

00:00:07.282 --> 00:00:10.752
A rule version identifies which logic was used.

00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:13.552
A timestamp records when cleaning occurred.

00:00:13.552 --> 00:00:16.467
Issue codes explain detected problems.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:19.452
Review status records the resolution state.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:24.007
These fields make the cleaning process reproducible and auditable.

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:28.792
Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:32.837
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention;

00:00:32.837 --> 00:00:35.307
it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:35.307 --> 00:00:42.000
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
